Hono server. Routes are registered in `src/index.ts`. Handlers stay thin; shared logic goes in `src/lib/`.

{{#if (eq pm "bun")}}`dev` and `start` run under Bun{{else}}`dev` and `start` run on Node through `tsx`, from `src/server.ts` (it serves the app of `src/index.ts` with `@hono/node-server`){{/if}} and listen on port {{#if (isMono)}}{{appPort appName}}{{else}}3000{{/if}}. The `PORT` environment variable overrides it.

The error handler in `src/app.ts` keeps the status and message of an `HTTPException` and answers any other error with a generic 500; the real error is always logged with its stack. It returns the message and stack only when `NODE_ENV=development`, so run `NODE_ENV=development {{runScript "dev"}}` to see them in responses. Throw `HTTPException` for errors meant for the client.
